<div class="container breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;›&nbsp; <a href="/#celebrities">Celebrities</a> &nbsp;›&nbsp; <a href="/celebrities/actors.html">Actors &amp; Artists</a> &nbsp;›&nbsp; Manju Warrier</div>
<section class="profile-hero"><div class="container profile-layout">
<div class="profile-photo" aria-label="Manju Warrier profile image"><img src="/celebrities/images/manju-warrier.jpg" alt="Manju Warrier profile portrait" width="381" height="535" loading="eager" decoding="async"><div class="photo-credit">Photo: Anees Kodiyathur / Wikimedia Commons — CC BY-SA 3.0</div></div>
<div><div class="eyebrow">KeralaCelebrities.com · Malayalam Cinema</div><h1>Manju Warrier</h1><p class="hero-intro"><strong>Manju Warrier</strong> is one of the most celebrated actresses associated with Malayalam cinema, known for a remarkable first phase in the 1990s, a long break from acting, and a widely recognised return to the screen in 2014.</p>
<div class="badges"><span class="badge">Malayalam Actress</span><span class="badge">Award Winner</span><span class="badge">Producer</span><span class="badge">Classical Dancer</span></div>
<div class="quick-facts"><div class="fact"><strong>Born</strong><span>10 September 1978</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Profession</strong><span>Actress, Producer, Dancer, Playback Singer</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Primary Cinema</strong><span>Malayalam</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Screen Debut</strong><span><em>Sakshyam</em> (1995)</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Major Comeback</strong><span><em>How Old Are You?</em> (2014)</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>State Award</strong><span>Best Actress for <em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em></span></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><div><div class="section-label">The story</div><h2>Who is Manju Warrier?</h2><p>Manju Warrier is an Indian actress, producer, classical dancer and playback singer who has worked predominantly in Malayalam cinema. Her career is notable for the extraordinary impact of her early films, her long absence from the screen and the strength of her return.</p><p>She began acting with <em>Sakshyam</em> in 1995 and quickly moved into leading roles. Films such as <em>Thooval Kottaram</em>, <em>Sallapam</em>, <em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em>, <em>Aaraam Thampuran</em>, <em>Kanmadam</em>, <em>Summer in Bethlehem</em> and <em>Pathram</em> established her as one of the defining female stars of 1990s Malayalam cinema.</p><p>After stepping away from acting, Warrier returned with <em>How Old Are You?</em> in 2014. The comeback opened a new chapter in her career, leading to acclaimed performances in films including <em>Udaharanam Sujatha</em>, <em>Aami</em>, <em>Lucifer</em>, <em>Prathi Poovankozhi</em> and the Tamil film <em>Asuran</em>.</p></div>
<aside class="story-card"><h3>At a glance</h3><ul><li>Born on 10 September 1978 in Nagercoil, Tamil Nadu.</li><li>Made her acting debut with <em>Sakshyam</em> in 1995.</li><li>Won the Kerala State Film Award for Best Actress for <em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em>.</li><li>Received a National Film Award Special Mention for <em>Kannezhuthi Pottum Thottu</em>.</li><li>Returned to cinema with <em>How Old Are You?</em> in 2014.</li><li>Made her Tamil film debut with <em>Asuran</em>.</li><li>Has also worked as a producer on selected projects.</li></ul></aside></div></section>
<section class="section alt"><div class="container"><div class="section-label">Career milestones</div><h2>A career defined by talent, absence and a remarkable return</h2><div class="timeline">
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1995</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>Sakshyam</h3><p>Manju Warrier made her screen debut with <em>Sakshyam</em>, beginning a short but extraordinarily influential first phase in Malayalam cinema.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1996</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>A breakthrough year</h3><p><em>Thooval Kottaram</em>, <em>Sallapam</em> and <em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em> established her as a leading actress. Her performance in <em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em> earned the Kerala State Film Award for Best Actress.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1997–98</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>Peak of the first era</h3><p>Films such as <em>Aaraam Thampuran</em>, <em>Kanmadam</em>, <em>Krishnagudiyil Oru Pranayakalathu</em>, <em>Pranayavarnangal</em> and <em>Summer in Bethlehem</em> strengthened her position as one of Malayalam cinema's most prominent stars.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1999</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>Kannezhuthi Pottum Thottu</h3><p>Her performance in <em>Kannezhuthi Pottum Thottu</em> brought a National Film Award Special Mention, marking a significant artistic high point of her first career phase.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1999–2014</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>A long break from acting</h3><p>After her early run of films, Warrier stepped away from the screen for many years. Her absence became an unusual and enduring part of her public story.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2014</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>How Old Are You?</h3><p>Warrier returned to cinema with <em>How Old Are You?</em>, beginning the second major phase of her acting career and receiving renewed audience and industry recognition.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2017–19</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>New-generation roles</h3><p><em>Udaharanam Sujatha</em>, <em>Aami</em>, <em>Lucifer</em> and <em>Prathi Poovankozhi</em> showed the range of her post-comeback career. She also entered Tamil cinema with <em>Asuran</em>.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2021–24</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>Acting and production</h3><p>She continued across Malayalam and Tamil cinema with projects including <em>The Priest</em>, <em>Chathur Mukham</em>, <em>Marakkar</em>, <em>Lalitham Sundaram</em>, <em>Ayisha</em>, <em>Vellari Pattanam</em>, <em>Footage</em>, <em>Vettaiyan</em> and <em>Viduthalai Part 2</em>.</p></div></div>
<div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2025–26</div><div class="timeline-content"><h3>Continuing across languages</h3><p>Her recent work includes <em>L2: Empuraan</em> and the Tamil action thriller <em>Mr. X</em>. She has also been announced for <em>Odiyan: The Age of Illusion</em>, expanding her current slate further.</p></div></div>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-label">Landmark cinema</div><h2>Films that define different sides of Manju Warrier</h2><p>These selections trace the major chapters of her career, from her 1990s breakthrough to her post-comeback work.</p><div class="film-grid">
<div class="film-card"><div class="year">1996</div><h3>Thooval Kottaram</h3><p>A key early performance that helped establish Warrier as a major young star.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">1996</div><h3>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</h3><p>An award-winning performance that brought her the Kerala State Film Award for Best Actress.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">1997</div><h3>Aaraam Thampuran</h3><p>A major commercial film from the peak of her first career phase.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">1998</div><h3>Kanmadam</h3><p>A memorable collaboration with Mohanlal that remains part of her landmark 1990s filmography.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">1999</div><h3>Kannezhuthi Pottum Thottu</h3><p>A critically recognised performance that earned a National Film Award Special Mention.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2014</div><h3>How Old Are You?</h3><p>The comeback film that opened the second major chapter of her screen career.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2017</div><h3>Udaharanam Sujatha</h3><p>A grounded role that earned major critical recognition during her post-comeback period.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2018</div><h3>Aami</h3><p>Warrier portrayed writer Kamala Surayya in a biographical drama.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2019</div><h3>Lucifer</h3><p>A major Malayalam commercial film in which she played Priyadarshini Ramdas.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2019</div><h3>Asuran</h3><p>Her Tamil debut brought a major performance opposite Dhanush.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2023</div><h3>Ayisha</h3><p>A Malayalam-Arabic bilingual film built around Warrier in the title role.</p></div><div class="film-card"><div class="year">2026</div><h3>Mr. X</h3><p>A Tamil action thriller featuring Warrier as Indira Varma.</p></div>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section alt"><div class="container"><div class="section-label">Awards &amp; recognition</div><h2>Honours across her career</h2><table class="award-table"><thead><tr><th>Award / Recognition</th><th>Year</th><th>Work / Note</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Kerala State Film Award — Best Actress</td><td>1996</td><td><em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em></td></tr><tr><td>National Film Award — Special Mention</td><td>1999</td><td><em>Kannezhuthi Pottum Thottu</em></td></tr><tr><td>Filmfare Awards South — Best Actress</td><td>Multiple years</td><td>Recognition across her Malayalam film career</td></tr><tr><td>SIIMA — Best Actress in a Leading Role</td><td>2015 &amp; 2020</td><td><em>How Old Are You?</em> and <em>Lucifer</em></td></tr><tr><td>Tamil Nadu State Film Award — Best Actress</td><td>2019</td><td><em>Asuran</em></td></tr><tr><td>Kerala Film Critics Association Awards</td><td>Multiple years</td><td>Recognition including <em>Udaharanam Sujatha</em> and <em>Prathi Poovankozhi</em></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><div><div class="section-label">Beyond acting</div><h2>Producer, dancer and performer</h2><p>Warrier's work extends beyond acting. She is also associated with classical dance and playback singing, and has taken on production responsibilities on selected films.</p><p>Her producer credits include projects such as <em>Kayattam</em>, <em>Chathur Mukham</em> and <em>Lalitham Sundaram</em>. This broader involvement reflects the expanding creative role she has taken during the second phase of her career.</p></div><aside class="story-card"><h3>Selected production work</h3><ul><li><em>Kayattam</em></li><li><em>Chathur Mukham</em></li><li><em>Lalitham Sundaram</em></li><li>Other selected creative projects</li></ul></aside></div></section>
<section class="section alt"><div class="container faq"><div class="section-label">Frequently asked questions</div><h2>Manju Warrier FAQ</h2>
<div class="faq-item"><h3>Who is Manju Warrier?</h3><p>Manju Warrier is an Indian actress, producer, classical dancer and playback singer known predominantly for Malayalam cinema.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>When did Manju Warrier make her acting debut?</h3><p>She made her acting debut with <em>Sakshyam</em> in 1995.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Which film won Manju Warrier the Kerala State Film Award for Best Actress?</h3><p>She won the award for her performance in <em>Ee Puzhayum Kadannu</em>.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Which film earned Manju Warrier a National Film Award Special Mention?</h3><p>She received the Special Mention for <em>Kannezhuthi Pottum Thottu</em>.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>What was Manju Warrier's comeback film?</h3><p><em>How Old Are You?</em> marked her return to cinema in 2014 after a long break from acting.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>What are some of Manju Warrier's recent films?</h3><p>Recent work includes <em>L2: Empuraan</em>, <em>Mr. X</em> and the upcoming <em>Odiyan: The Age of Illusion</em>.</p></div>
</div></section>
